## 🎯 Day 37 Objective

The register (Day 34) tracks what *could* go wrong. This playbook is for when it *does*. AI incidents aren't classic security incidents — a model can be "up" and fully "secure" while quietly discriminating, hallucinating harmful advice, or leaking training data through its outputs. Standard SEV runbooks miss these entirely.

Today I built an **AI Incident Response Playbook**: what counts as an AI incident, how to triage severity, who does what, the step-by-step runbook, ready-to-use comms templates, and the regulatory clocks (EU AI Act, GDPR) that start ticking the moment you detect one. This closes the loop — incidents feed learnings straight back into the register and model cards.

