## 🌪️ What Counts as an AI Incident

An AI incident is any event where an AI system causes, or is about to cause, harm, rights impact, legal exposure, or loss of trust. Categories most IR plans miss:

| Type | Example |
|------|---------|
| **Harmful output** | Model gives dangerous medical/legal/financial advice; generates toxic or defamatory content |
| **Discriminatory outcome** | Systematic bias detected in a live decision system |
| **Data leakage via model** | Model regurgitates PII/secrets from training data or context; prompt-injection exfiltration |
| **Hallucination with consequence** | Fabricated fact drives a real-world action (wrong refund, wrong diagnosis) |
| **Prompt injection / jailbreak** | Attacker manipulates an agent into unauthorized actions |
| **Model drift / degradation** | Silent accuracy decay causes a spike in wrong decisions |
| **Unauthorized / rogue use** | Shadow AI, or a system used outside its approved scope |
| **Third-party model failure** | Vendor changes/deprecates a model, breaking behavior or safety |
| **Autonomy failure** | An agent takes a consequential action with no human review path |

