## 🚨 Severity Tiers

| Tier | Criteria | Response SLA | Who's engaged |
|------|----------|:------------:|---------------|
| **SEV-1 — Critical** | Active harm to people, rights violation at scale, regulatory-reportable, or safety impact | **Immediate** — halt system | Full IRT + exec + legal/DPO |
| **SEV-2 — High** | Serious risk, limited harm occurring, or high reputational exposure | **< 4 hours** | IRT + AI gov lead + comms |
| **SEV-3 — Moderate** | Contained issue, no ongoing harm, workaround exists | **< 1 business day** | System owner + AI gov lead |
| **SEV-4 — Low** | Minor, no harm, quality/near-miss | **Next cycle** | System owner |

> **Declare high, downgrade later.** Under-calling an AI incident is the expensive mistake — you lose containment time and blow regulatory clocks. Start high; downgrade once you understand blast radius.

